Translation patch: `sql_trusted` (new module: the trust boundary of `Value::as_sql` and `Params`)

Change: Adds `src/sql_trusted.rs`, declared `pub(crate) mod sql_trusted` in `lib.rs`: one function per `std` operation that `Value::as_sql` and `Params` use and Aeneas does not model, each body being that single call: `String::from(&str)`, `s.extend(t.chars())`, one `format!` per format string of `as_sql` (`{}` of i64/u64/f32/f64, the date, datetime, time and `{:02X}` formats), and the six `HashMap<Vec<u8>, Value>` operations `Params` needs (`default`, `contains_key`, `insert`, `get`, `remove`, and `into_iter().collect()` into a `Vec` of entries).
Why: The module is `opaque` in Cargo.toml, so the trusted surface of this code is exactly this list of Rust functions, each with a Lean model or axiom in `FunsExternal.lean` (the pattern of patch 40). Aeneas does not model `fmt`/`format!`, `String`'s methods, or `HashMap` (std, not this crate). A separate module from `value::convert::trusted` keeps these helpers apart from the value conversions.
Behaviour: Unchanged: the module is not used until the next patches.

